# Canvas Core

Shared geometry engine for the 14 visual canvas tools. Spec:
[`docs/modules/CANVAS_CORE.md`](../../docs/modules/CANVAS_CORE.md). Measured defect
inventory, external traps, QoL list and blind spots:
[`docs/audit/canvas-core-audit-2026-09-06.md`](../../docs/audit/canvas-core-audit-2026-09-06.md).

**Status 2026-09-07:** Waves 0–4 landed (CanvasWrapper, LogoContainer, denser print
design widths for ~200 PPI browser-safe export, print-family + fluid/intrinsic tool
migrations, A4 + aspect registry, layout-matrix proportion guards). Read the audit for
measured defects that motivated this work.

## Read before touching any canvas tool

Pre-fix measurements (2026-09-06) that motivated Canvas Core — **Waves 0–4 shipped**;
treat these as historical defects, not current behaviour:

1. **Logo sizing was not canvas-relative** (81% / 58% / 44% across paper sizes). Fixed via
   `LogoContainer` % caps inside `CanvasWrapper`.
2. **Previews never scaled up** (`FitWidthFrame` was scale-down only). Use `CanvasWrapper`
   with an explicit `maxScale` (default 2); legacy `FitWidthFrame` still caps at 1.
3. **Letter print exports were ~144 PPI.** Design width is now 850px; target raster **1700px
   (~200 PPI)**. Do **not** push to 2550/~300 PPI in-browser — Chromium `html-to-image` OOMs
   on letter sheets (verified in export smoke). Check real PNG dimensions.
4. **The export pipeline is already unified.** No tool imports `html-to-image` or `jspdf`
   directly. Do not "consolidate" it again — remaining work is geometry and density policy.

Session lessons: [`docs/audit/session-knowledge-2026-09-07-canvas-core.md`](../../docs/audit/session-knowledge-2026-09-07-canvas-core.md).

## Hard rules

1. **Never `maxWidth: 100%` on `[data-export-root]`.** Fixed `width` + `height` +
   `maxWidth: 100%` desyncs paper aspect from type scale. Scale with a transform on a
   **parent**; `capture.ts` zeroes `transform` on the clone. (Inner non-root wrappers,
   e.g. a QR plate box, may still use `maxWidth: 100%`.)
2. **`container-type: size` applies size containment in both axes.** Use it only where
   height is known. Content-driven canvases (pulse-poll, board-banner strips,
   logo-builder rectangle) must use `inline-size`, where **`cqh` is unavailable**.
   Getting this wrong collapses the canvas to zero height.
3. **`cqw` resolves against the nearest container ancestor.** Declare a `container-name`
   on the canvas root and reference it, so a nested container cannot silently re-base the
   scale. Prefer parent-% logo caps when a container may be missing.
4. **Container queries do not improve export fidelity.** `inlineComputedStylesForCapture`
   flattens computed values to px on the clone, so `cqw` and design-px produce identical
   rasters. The win is authoring consistency — one proportional rule replacing three
   scaling systems. Export **quality** is governed by pixel ratio and design width.
5. **`CAPTURE_STYLE_PROPS` is an allowlist.** It does **not** include `borderWidth`,
   `borderStyle`, `aspectRatio`, `flexBasis`, `flexGrow`, `flexShrink`, `backgroundSize`,
   `backgroundPosition` or `boxShadow`. `cqw` in any of those will not survive capture.
   Extend the allowlist before relying on them.
6. **Size from layout px, never rects or DPR.** `buildHtmlToImageOptions` uses
   `offsetWidth`/`offsetHeight`, so exports are identical on every display. Do not switch
   to `getBoundingClientRect()` (transform-scaled) or read `window.devicePixelRatio`.
7. **Verify export density against artifacts, not comments.** Check real PNG dimensions
   before claiming a DPI target is met.
9. **Brand Kit stays the multi-union seam.** Proportions must not override
   `resolveCanvasTokens` density, type scale, alignment bias or typefaces.
10. **One logo aspect lock cannot fit all variants.** Wide lockups ~4.4:1, standard
   lockups 2.5:1, marks 1:1. Resolve `AssetBounds` per variant off
   `resolveBrandLogoPresentation`.
11. **Print supporting type is engine-owned.** Letter/tabloid tools use
   `resolvePrintPageLayout` (or `printPageScaledTokens`, which caps inset/gap).
   Never hand-tune `metaSize = subtitleFontSizePx + N`. Meta stays ≤ ~2.6% of
   design width; pack fixed-height stacks with `justify-content: flex-start`
   (QR/footer can use `mt-auto`) — do not `justify-between` meta into
   `overflow: hidden`.

## External traps

- **Canvas taint:** `duotone-photo.ts` loads photos without `crossOrigin` and swallows the
  `SecurityError`, so a cross-origin photo silently exports without its duotone. Safe only
  because photos are local uploads today.
- **CDN assets:** logos render via plain `<img src="/assets/...">`. Serving `/assets` from
  another origin without CORS makes exports lose the logo while the preview still looks
  correct.
- **Font race:** `awaitDocumentFontsReady` times out after 5s and proceeds silently with
  fallback metrics. `document.fonts.ready` also resolves early for faces not yet
  requested (`next/font/local` loads lazily).
- **Silent brand substitution:** `SafeLogoImage` falls back to the UnionOps mark
  `onError`, so a broken local logo exports the **platform** brand with no warning.
- **No bleed or crop marks:** PDFs are generated at exact trim size.
- **PDF is JPEG at 0.92, no CMYK** — flat brand fields can band at a commercial printer.

## Testing

- `expectPreviewFitsColumn` asserts **width only**, which is why the logo and fit defects
  pass CI today. Add height, aspect, proportion and minimum-font assertions.
- Run canvas suites with `--workers=1`. They are flaky in parallel on this machine and
  pass serially.
- `compareRasters` compares preview against export, **not** against an approved design.
  Capture reference PNGs per layout class before a refactor or consistent drift passes
  silently.
- French copy runs 15–25% longer and auto-fits smaller — cover at least one FR row per
  layout class.

## Shipping obligations

New sizes or canvas capabilities are steward-visible: add a `/updates` note
([`whats-new.mdc`](whats-new.mdc)) and EN/FR labels whose **claims** match
([`i18n-public-copy.mdc`](i18n-public-copy.mdc)).

## Superseded rules

Landing Canvas Core Wave 0 must rewrite, in the same change:

- [`comms-visual-system.mdc`](comms-visual-system.mdc) — drop "Do not collapse all tools
  into one layout engine" and "Do not port Board FitWidth to every tool"
- [`solidarity-posters.mdc`](solidarity-posters.mdc) — `FitWidthFrame` becomes
  `CanvasWrapper`
- [`tool-editor-ux.mdc`](tool-editor-ux.mdc) — reset the migration register as tools land

[`export-engine-parity.mdc`](export-engine-parity.mdc) is **not** superseded: raster PDF,
text PDF and Office remain separate writers. `useCanvasExport` unifies the raster lane only.
